Title: Hundreds of fish dead in Hartlepool pond after temperatures rise
Date: 2025-07-13
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Labour MP Jonathan Brash', 'Text': 'He said: "They\'re currently aerating the water to boost oxygen levels and are testing the water quality.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 9, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 85}}, {'Speaker': 'Labour MP Jonathan Brash', 'Text': '"The initial view is that the recent hot weather reduced oxygen levels and increased ammonia - a dangerous mix for the fish.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 10, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 111}}, {'Speaker': 'Labour MP Jonathan Brash', 'Text': '"The good news is there\'s still a living fish population in the pond, and we\'ve now moved into the recovery phase."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 11, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 100}}], 'Description': [{'Description': 'Volunteers have pulled 173 lbs (78 kg) of dead fish out of a park pond after a hike in water temperatures.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 1, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 85}}, {'Description': 'Residents spotted hundreds of the fish floating on the surface of the pond at Rossmere Park, Hartlepool.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 2, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 91}}, {'Description': 'Hartlepool Borough Councillor Quewone Bailey-Fleet said that three local men removed the dead fish from the pond and have now committed to volunteering long-term to help maintain it.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 7, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 157}}, {'Description': 'Mr Brash met with the council and Environment Agency teams at the pond.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 8, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 62}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': 'A man is putting a black bag of dead fish into the back of a Highway Maintenance van.'}]}
